---
title: DeliveryStatus - what becomes of one guest's confirmation (every one ends in exactly one final state)
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  [*] --> Held: reserve() inside the booking's transaction
  Held --> REJECTED: queue full or closing - counted rejected, answer notificationFailed true
  Held --> [*]: rollback - release(), never counted, never sent
  Held --> QUEUED: COMMIT, then publish() (accepted += 1)
  QUEUED --> SENDING: a worker takes it (place freed)
  QUEUED --> DROPPED: shutdown after the drain limit, or --no-drain (named in the log)
  SENDING --> SENT: the sender returned (completed += 1)
  SENDING --> SENDING: attempt failed, attempts left - wait 0.5 s, 1 s, ... in the same worker
  SENDING --> FAILED: last attempt failed or timed out (failed += 1, logged)
  SENDING --> DROPPED: shutdown during the retry wait
  REJECTED --> [*]
  SENT --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
  DROPPED --> [*]
  note right of SENDING
    in flight - at most one job per worker,
    accepted = completed + failed + dropped + queued + in flight
  end note
